### Literature Search Expansion Summary: Round 2 (Decisive Computational Controls)

The literature search for the Rub' al-Khali dark-proteome manuscript targeting ***Nature Communications*** has been expanded, focusing specifically on small decisive computational controls to resolve the findings raised in the Round 1 review ([`reviews/darkmatter-2026-10-13/round1/response.md`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/reviews/darkmatter-2026-10-13/round1/response.md)) and [`manuscript/main.tex`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/manuscript/main.tex).

All sources were vetted following [`SOURCE_AUDIT.md`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/SOURCE_AUDIT.md) and [`verified_sources.tsv`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/verified_sources.tsv). Retained full texts were downloaded **only** under [`resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2), with every document's embedded DOI and title programmatically verified against its intended source. Inaccessible subscription leads are explicitly labelled in the manifest. No manuscript or analysis files were altered.

