### Core Findings & Decisive Computational Controls

```
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                         DECISIVE COMPUTATIONAL CONTROL ARCHITECTURE                                 |
+------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Methodological Vulnerability       | Decisive Computational Control & Primary Provenance           |
+------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| 1. Spurious / Shadow ORFs          | - EasyGene RNY codon-bias background model (Larsen 2003)       |
|    (Overlapping & antisense frames)| - GOS overlap exclusion thresholds (Yooseph 2007)             |
|                                    | - Spurio tBLASTn stop-codon blizzard test (Höps 2018)         |
|                                    | - Frame-specific OLGenie selection modeling (Ardern 2020)     |
+------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| 2. AntiFam Contamination           | - AntiFam 7.0 profile HMM screening (Eberhardt 2012)          |
|    (ncRNA & spurious translations) | - AlphaFold/ESMFold low-pLDDT structural triage               |
|                                    |   (Monzon 2022; Orr & Bateman 2026)                           |
+------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| 3. Divergence-Confounded dN/dS     | - Divergence-stratified matching on dS, length, and GC        |
|    & Short Alignment Variance      |   (Rocha 2006; Kryazhimskiy 2008; Mugal 2014)                 |
|                                    | - Maximum likelihood codon models (Yang & Nielsen 2000)       |
|                                    | - Length-dependent variance bounds (Nekrutenko 2002)          |
+------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| 4. Protein Absence vs. Nucleotide  | - Nucleotide 6-frame alignment rescue (Panaroo; Tonkin-Hill)  |
|    Presence in Isolates / MAGs     | - Fast protein-to-genome mapping with miniprot (Li 2023)      |
|                                    | - PPanGGOLiN synteny & contig-edge graph (Gautreau 2020)      |
|                                    | - Chimeric MAG artifact filtering (Shaiber & Eren 2019)       |
+------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| 5. Foldseek Score Normalisation    | - Explicit decomposition of TM_query vs TM_aligned            |
|    & Domain Architecture Controls  |   (Foldseek; van Kempen 2024; Xu & Zhang 2010)                |
|                                    | - Deep-learning domain segmentation (Merizo, Chainsaw, TED)   |
|                                    |   (Lau 2023; Wells 2024; Lau 2024)                            |
|                                    | - Calibrated positive & decoy retrieval (Barrio-Hernandez)    |
+------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### 1. Spurious & Shadow ORFs in Metagenomic Gene Prediction
- **Biophysical Mechanism:** Primary coding sequences exhibit periodic **RNY codon bias** (purine-any-pyrimidine). Because universal stop codons begin with T, the reverse complement of an RNY sequence exhibits a strong statistical deficit of stop codons in frame $-1$ and $-2$ ([Larsen & Krogh 2003](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/larsen_2003_easygene_shadow_orfs.xml)). Unconstrained gene callers (Prodigal in `-p meta` mode without organism-specific RBS training; [Hyatt et al. 2010](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/hyatt_2010_prodigal_gene_recognition.xml)) regularly predict long shadow ORFs on the opposite strand.
- **Controls:**
  1. *Overlap Geometry Exclusion:* Apply the Global Ocean Sampling overlap filter ([Yooseph et al. 2007](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/yooseph_2007_gos_shadow_orfs.xml)), discarding same-strand overlaps $\ge 60$ bp and opposite-strand overlaps $\ge 50$ bp / 120 bp.
  2. *Stop-Codon Blizzard Test (Spurio):* Cross-taxa `tblastn` against nucleotide databases flags spurious proteins when homologous translated regions collapse into a "blizzard" of nonsense mutations ([Höps et al. 2018](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/hops_2018_spurio_gene_unprediction.xml)).
  3. *Frame-Specific Selection (OLGenie):* Authentic overlapping/antisense genes require frame-stratified $dN/dS$ proof to confirm independent constraint ([Ardern et al. 2020](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/ardern_2020_antisense_proteins_prokaryotes.xml); [Nelson et al. 2020](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/nelson_2020_olgenie_overlapping_genes.xml)).

#### 2. AntiFam & ncRNA Translation Screening
- **Controls:**
  1. *Profile HMM Screening:* `hmmsearch` against AntiFam release 7.0 ([Eberhardt et al. 2012](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/eberhardt_2012_antifam_spurious_orfs.xml)) purges dark families derived from non-coding RNAs (16S, 23S, 5S rRNA, tRNA, tmRNA), riboswitches, and cloning vectors.
  2. *Structural Triage:* Spurious proteins exhibit characteristic structural failure modes in AlphaFold2 and ESMFold: mean pLDDT < 50, disordered coils, and lack of a hydrophobic core ([Monzon et al. 2022](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/monzon_2022_antifam_alphafold_spurious.xml); [Orr & Bateman 2026](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/orr_2026_antifam_esmfold_spurious.xml)). P4's confidence gate (pLDDT $\ge 0.70$) intrinsically excludes these non-coding artifacts.

#### 3. Divergence-Confounded $dN/dS$ & Short Alignment Variance
- **Theoretical Basis:** Pairwise $dN/dS$ is fundamentally time-dependent in bacteria ([Rocha et al. 2006](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.08.037)). At shallow divergence ($dS < 0.2$), slightly deleterious mutations segregate as transient polymorphisms, elevating $dN/dS$ toward 1.0 even under strict negative selection ([Kryazhimskiy & Plotkin 2008](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/kryazhimskiy_2008_population_genetics_dnds.xml); [Mugal et al. 2014](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/mugal_2014_temporal_dynamics_dnds.xml)). In short sequences (<100 aa), low counts of synonymous sites create extreme sampling variance and division-by-zero bias ([Nekrutenko et al. 2002](https://doi.org/10.1101/gr.200901)), while counting models (NG86) underestimate multiple hits under GC bias ([Yang & Nielsen 2000](https://doi.org/10.1093/oxfordjournals.molbev.a026236)).
- **Controls:**
  1. *Stratified Reporting:* Disclose $dN/dS$ within narrow $dS$ strata ($dS \in [0.1, 0.3]$, $[0.3, 0.5]$, $[0.5, 0.8]$), explicitly noting that in the lowest divergence stratum ($dS \le 0.10$), dark and annotated controls have indistinguishable medians (0.582 vs 0.580).
  2. *Joint Coarsened Exact Matching:* Match dark and control families jointly on $dS$, alignment length, GC content, and lineage to eliminate residual confounding.

#### 4. Protein Absence vs. Nucleotide Presence in Basin Isolates
- **Mechanism:** In comparisons between MAGs and 722 cultured isolate genomes, apparent protein absence (only 15.8% reciprocal hits for dark proteins) often reflects gene caller omission, contig boundary truncation, or frameshift sequencing errors rather than true physical absence from the isolate's chromosome ([Shaiber & Eren 2019](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/shaiber_2019_composite_mags_quality.xml); [Majernik et al. 2025](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/majernik_2025_pansweep_misassembly.xml)).
- **Controls:**
  1. *miniprot / tBLASTn Alignment:* Align all 1,507 dark MAG proteins directly against the nucleotide contigs of the 722 cultured genomes using `miniprot` ([Li 2023](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/li_2023_miniprot_protein_to_genome.xml)) to rescue unannotated or frameshifted genes.
  2. *Graph-Based Nucleotide Rescue:* Employ graph-based pangenome rescue principles ([Tonkin-Hill et al. 2020](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/tonkin_hill_2020_panaroo_pangenome_polishing.xml); [Gautreau et al. 2020](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/gautreau_2020_ppanggolin_pangenome_graph.xml)) to separate true biological absence from assembly/annotation fragmentation.

#### 5. Foldseek Score Normalisation & Domain Architecture Controls
- **Score Normalisation Mathematics:**
  Foldseek ([van Kempen et al. 2024](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/vankempen_2024_foldseek_structure_search.xml)) calculates structural alignment significance where the TM-score can be normalised by:
  - Query length ($TM_{query}$): Checks if the whole query protein matches the target.
  - Aligned length ($TM_{aligned}$): Evaluates local structural fold identity.
  In multidomain proteins, query-length normalisation penalises single-domain matches ($TM_{query} < 0.5$), falsely claiming whole-protein darkness, whereas aligned-length normalisation reveals known fold domains ($TM_{aligned} \ge 0.5$; [Xu & Zhang 2010](https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btq066)). The 936 P4 candidate models are locally familiar and globally unmatched.
- **Controls:**
  1. *Domain Segmentation:* Run **Merizo** ([Lau et al. 2023](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/lau_2023_merizo_domain_segmentation.xml)) or **Chainsaw** ([Wells et al. 2024](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/wells_2024_chainsaw_domain_segmentation.xml)) to segment candidate models into discrete compact units prior to Foldseek searches, following The Encyclopedia of Domains ([Lau et al. 2024](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/lau_2024_ted_encyclopedia_of_domains.xml)).
  2. *Retrieval Calibration:* Calibrate positive controls using predicted ESMFold models matched on length, pLDDT, and secondary structure composition with close sequence homologs excluded ([Barrio-Hernandez et al. 2023](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/barrio_hernandez_2023_afdb_clusters_retrieval.xml)).

