### *Nature Communications* Author Requirements for Reproducible Computational Biology

Publisher pages from Nature Portfolio and Springer Nature were retrieved and retained:
- [`nature_portfolio_reporting_standards.html`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/nature_portfolio_reporting_standards.html)
- [`springernature_research_data_policy.html`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/springernature_research_data_policy.html)
- [`nature_portfolio_peer_review_policy.html`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/nature_portfolio_peer_review_policy.html)
- [`nature_portfolio_authorship_policy.html`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/round2/nature_portfolio_authorship_policy.html)

**Key Author Mandates:**
1. **Reporting Summary:** Completion of the official Nature Portfolio Reporting Summary (covering sample size pre-determination, data exclusion criteria, blinding, replication, exact $n$, test statistics, degrees of freedom, and exact two-sided $p$-values).
2. **Code Availability:** Dedicated statement before References; mandatory deposition of custom analysis scripts in a persistent, DOI-minting repository (**Zenodo** or **Code Ocean**) with clear installation guides, OS/dependency definitions (`uv` / `environment.yml`), and an OSI-approved open-source license. Custom computational workflows are subject to peer review.
3. **Data Availability:** Mandatory pre-publication deposition and public release of raw shotgun sequencing reads (ENA/SRA), assembled MAG contigs (GenBank/ENA), novel protein sequences (UniProt), and predicted structures (wwPDB/AlphaFold DB), with formal data citations in the reference list.

